From d7f23fd02e9d02b6d18281d5b7c1448190eaecdc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 05:51:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1143/1157] fix(update-pause): withdraw a blocked clarify so
 the turn pauses for a core update [daveey]

A Desktop turn waiting in clarify never reaches a step boundary, so the
drainer's pause request ran out its 180s budget and the update cut the
turn, which resumed with the crash note (example-hub 2026-10-30 05:37,
session 20261030_045045_3394a8: a 41-min clarify; t_01a18ac84e3491a9).

A clarify_early provider, installed with the per-turn boundary hook,
withdraws the pending clarify (status paused_for_update, notice says to
re-ask) when a pause is requested for a turn the next backend
auto-continues; the hook then pauses at the boundary right after it.
